{"name":"Caddies Silk","hex":"#3e354d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"caddies","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of caddie","plural of caddy"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of caddy","third-person singular simple present indicative of caddie"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caddies"},{"term":"silk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fine fiber excreted by the silkworm or other arthropod (such as a spider).","A thread or yarn made from silk fibers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To develop silk.","To remove the silk from (corn)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caddie","blocks":[{"text":"In golf, a caddie is a companion to the player, providing both practical support and strategic guidance on the course. Caddies are responsible for carrying the player’s bag, managing clubs, and assisting with basic course maintenance like repairing divots and raking bunkers. Caddies may also offer insight on course strategy, such as club selection, reading greens, and evaluating weather conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Phil_%26_Jim_%22Bones%22_MacKay_2014.jpg/330px-Phil_%26_Jim_%22Bones%22_MacKay_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caddie","wikidata":"Q1064569"},{"title":"Silk","blocks":[{"text":"Silk is a natural protein fiber, some forms of which can be woven or knitted into textiles. The protein fiber of silk is composed mainly of fibroin (75-80%) and a smaller coating of sericin (20-25%). It is most commonly produced from the cocoons of certain insect larvae. The best-known silk is obtained from the cocoons of the larvae of the mulberry silkworm Bombyx mori, which are reared in captivity (sericulture)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Silk_raw_01a.jpg/330px-Silk_raw_01a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silk","wikidata":"Q37681"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/TheCaddie.jpg/500px-TheCaddie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/TheCaddie.jpg/500px-TheCaddie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A caddie plies his trade. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATheCaddie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Imaginative_Marguerite_Martyn_drawing_of_Forest_Park_Golf_Course%2C_St._Louis%2C_in_1914.jpg/500px-Imaginative_Marguerite_Martyn_drawing_of_Forest_Park_Golf_Course%2C_St._Louis%2C_in_1914.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Imaginative_Marguerite_Martyn_drawing_of_Forest_Park_Golf_Course%2C_St._Louis%2C_in_1914.jpg/1280px-Imaginative_Marguerite_Martyn_drawing_of_Forest_Park_Golf_Course%2C_St._Louis%2C_in_1914.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Imaginative_Marguerite_Martyn_drawing_of_Forest_Park_Golf_Course%2C_St._Louis%2C_in_1914.jpg/500px-Imaginative_Marguerite_Martyn_drawing_of_Forest_Park_Golf_Course%2C_St._Louis%2C_in_1914.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Imaginative drawing by journalist Marguerite Martyn of a couple at the Forest Park Golf Course, Forest Road, Missouri, in 1914, while a caddie leans against a tree.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImaginative_Marguerite_Martyn_drawing_of_Forest_Park_Golf_Course%2C_St._Louis%2C_in_1914.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Golf_caddy.JPG/500px-